-- Ikada Why do we need a subquery?
Because you generally cannot directly filter a window-function result in the same WHERE clause where it is calculated

The pattern is:
Step 1 -> calculate window function
Step 2 -> put it in subquery/CTE
Step 3 -> filter the result

╰┈➤ Another Important Pattern: Find Duplicate Records 
SELECT * FROM (
    SELECT
        id, email,
        ROW_NUMBER() OVER(
            PARTITION BY email
            ORDER BY id) AS rn
    FROM customers
) t
WHERE rn > 1; -- This identifies duplicate records while preserving the original rows(Common in data celaning/ETL)


